Package: SCP
Type: Package
Title: Simulation-Based Circadian Power Analysis with K-harmonic LRT
Version: 0.4.55
Date: 2026-06-04
Authors@R: person("Thien Quy", "Pham",
    role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "quythien14@gmail.com",
    comment = c(affiliation = "University of Pittsburgh"))
Maintainer: Thien Quy Pham <quythien14@gmail.com>
URL: https://github.com/quythien/SCP
BugReports: https://github.com/quythien/SCP/issues
Description: Simulation-based power analysis for circadian transcriptomics
    studies. Empirical parameter distributions (amplitude, noise, phase,
    proportion rhythmic) are estimated from a pilot dataset, and power is
    evaluated for rhythmicity detection and differential-rhythm tests
    (DR, DP, DM) across a range of study designs. Detection uses a unified
    cosinor F-test detect_cosinor(K), with K = 1 for the single-harmonic
    case and K = 2 for the two-harmonic (ultradian) extension. A bootstrap
    design-grid optimiser is included for design comparison under pilot
    uncertainty.
